If a `Dependant` has `parent_oauth_scopes` but `own_oauth_scopes` is empty, and it has no sub-dependencies that use scopes, and `security_scopes_param_name` is None, then `_uses_scopes` will be `False`.

If `_uses_scopes` is `False`, `cache_key` uses `()`, regardless of `self.oauth_scopes` (which includes `parent_oauth_scopes`).

So if we have:
Route 1: A -> B (B has no scopes)
Route 2: C (scopes=['read']) -> B (B inherits scopes=['read'])

For Route 1:
B is created. `B.parent_oauth_scopes = []`, `B.own_oauth_scopes = []`. `B._uses_scopes = False`. `B.cache_key = (B.call, (), B.scope)`.

