B is created. `B.parent_oauth_scopes = ['read']`, `B.own_oauth_scopes = []`. `B._uses_scopes = False`. `B.cache_key = (B.call, (), B.scope)`.

Wait! The `cache_key` for B is the SAME in both cases!

So when `get_dependant` is called for Route 2, it will find the B from Route 1 in the `dependency_cache` and return it.

But the B from Route 1 has `parent_oauth_scopes = []`.
The B for Route 2 SHOULD have `parent_oauth_scopes = ['read']`.

This is exactly the bug.

